The 1930 Gurmukhi text of Gurushabad Ratnakar Mahan Kosh
(Bhai Kahan Singh Nabha) is in the public domain.

The English text (data/entries/en.json) is the English edition of
the Mahan Kosh published by Punjabi University, Patiala (2006–2011).
It is © Punjabi University, Patiala, and is included in SikhLibrary
with the University's written permission. It is NOT licensed under
CC BY 4.0. Any use of it outside SikhLibrary requires Punjabi
University's own permission. The machine translations into other
languages are made from that English text, and the same applies to
them.

Sikhi.io's own contributions (the Hindi text, the JSON packaging,
and the viewer in site/) are released under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may use, share, and adapt those contributions, including
commercially, if you give appropriate credit.

Whatever you use, you must follow the license of each organization
it comes from. Any organization can ask for the removal of texts it
owns by writing to akaal@sikhi.io.

Suggested attribution:

  Mahan Kosh multilingual dataset, from Bhai Kahan Singh Nabha,
  Gurushabad Ratnakar Mahan Kosh (1930); English edition
  © Punjabi University, Patiala (2006–2011), used with permission.
  Packaged by Sikhi.io (https://sikhi.io/dictionary), in honour of
  Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji.

Machine-translated languages have not been reviewed by native
speakers or subject scholars.
